ine polyphosphates by cultured adrenomedullary vascular endothelial cells</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><volume>273</volume><fpage>C918</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9316413</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-co-2-261"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mateo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rotllan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Miras-Portugal</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Suramin &#x02013; a powerful inhibitor of neural ecto-diadenosine polyphosphate hydrolase</article-title><source>Br J Pharmacol</source><volume>119</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8872348</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-co-2-261"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McLennan</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Dinucleoside polyphosphates &#x02013; friends or foe?</article-title><source>Pharmacol Ther</source><volume>87</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>89</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11007992</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-co-2-261"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Milder</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Moses</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hart</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>The lacrimal apparatus</article-title><source>Adler&#x02019;s Physiology of the eye</source><edition>8th ed</edition><publisher-loc>St Louis</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Mosby</publisher-name><fpage>15/35</fpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-co-2-261"><mixed-citation publication-type="jour